!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/meta-picks.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/meta.tn"
@doc:"""
  A meta layer holding one slot of each by-name spelling, so a schema importing it is where both are judged. `orders`
  maps identifiers to `order` records; `rpick.m` is typed `meta.ref<order>`, naming a value of `order`, which an importing
  schema holds only as a key of an entry built with `orders` (`os.o1`); `pick.t` is typed `meta.ref<record>`, naming a
  record type of the importing schema's own closure, which holds this layer's entries: `order` itself is a record type
  there, a member of `meta.ref<record>` and no value. An entry built with a namespace type is a value, not a type, and a
  processor that binds
  binds each value of its map to a host class of its own: the records `order`, `rpick` and `pick`.
  """
!schema {
  order  => { id: text }
  orders => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: order }
  rpick  => { m: meta.ref<order> }
  rpicks => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: rpick }
  pick   => { t: meta.ref<meta.record> }
  picks  => !meta.namespace { key_type: meta.identifier  value_type: pick }
}
